media: sun50i-h713-hdmirx: hold the capture enable until it sticks

0121 sets the capture enable after a republished descriptor, and the first
resolution change works: capture 1280x720, scaler 0x3200AAAA, PROC 1280x720 ->
1920x1080, full picture on the panel. The second change comes up black, and the
log says why -- "Capture direkt freigegeben, nach 0 ms" while 0x06940928 reads
0x60020438 a moment later. The write lands and the firmware clears it again in
its own sequence.

So keep setting it until it holds. Three reads 50 ms apart, up to the same
timeout as before; when the write takes, the bit is stable from the first read,
and when it does not, it is clear again within 100 ms. The source switch stays
as the fallback for the case where it never holds.

diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-07 23:00:28.686632183 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-07 23:00:28.693923580 +0200
@@ -1622,18 +1622,49 @@
 	 * is wrong -- and the log says which of the two happened.
 	 */
 	if (!erste) {
-		int ret = h713_hdmirx_capture_enable(rx);
+		/*
+		 * Setting the bit once is not enough: the firmware clears it
+		 * again a little later in its own sequence, so a write that is
+		 * only a few milliseconds early is undone and the capture stays
+		 * off. Keep setting it until it has held for a while, then stop.
+		 *
+		 * "Held" is three reads across 150 ms. Measured: when the write
+		 * takes, the bit is stable from the first read; when it does
+		 * not, it is clear again within 100 ms.
+		 */
+		ktime_t start = ktime_get();
+		unsigned int stabil = 0;
+		unsigned int val;
+		int ret = 0;
+
+		do {
+			if (regmap_read(rx->incap, H713_INCAP_ENABLE_Y, &val))
+				break;
+
+			if (val & H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT) {
+				if (++stabil >= 3) {
+					dev_info(rx->dev,
+						 "Freigabe: Capture direkt freigegeben, kein Quellenwechsel, nach %lld ms\n",
+						 ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start));
+					return;
+				}
+			} else {
+				stabil = 0;
+				ret = h713_hdmirx_capture_enable(rx);
+				if (ret)
+					break;
+			}
+			msleep(50);
+		} while (ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start) < H713_REARM_TIMEOUT_MS);
 
 		if (ret)
 			dev_warn(rx->dev,
 				 "Freigabe: Capture-Freigabe nicht schreibbar: %d\n",
 				 ret);
-		else if (h713_hdmirx_wait_enable(rx, "Capture direkt freigegeben, kein Quellenwechsel"))
-			return;
-
-		dev_warn(rx->dev,
-			 "Freigabe: direkte Freigabe hat nach %u ms nicht gegriffen; Quellenwechsel als Rueckfall -- der baut die Fensterkette neu und verliert dabei die Geometrie (doku/nachtlog/S7)\n",
-			 H713_REARM_TIMEOUT_MS);
+		else
+			dev_warn(rx->dev,
+				 "Freigabe: direkte Freigabe hat nach %u ms nicht gehalten; Quellenwechsel als Rueckfall -- der baut die Fensterkette neu und verliert dabei die Geometrie (doku/nachtlog/S7)\n",
+				 H713_REARM_TIMEOUT_MS);
 	}
 
 	if (h713_hdmirx_switch_source(rx))
